; Splitting into N partitions needs N-1 boundaries, and a partition that ends up
; empty puts one just outside the space, at the step beyond the induction start.
; Each loop below starts at the extreme of its iteration direction, where that
; step wraps to the far end of the type and still compares as in range, so the
; empty partition would come out covering the whole type. All four run a single
; iteration, so there is nothing to divide either way.

